{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002@rel:R19-11#b413f079","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R19-11","content":"If multiple operations are mapped to the same RunnableEn- tity , and [SWS_Rte_04522] requires a call serialization, then a single queue is imple- mented for invocations coming from any of the operations.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:19+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002@rel:R20-11#b413f079","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R20-11","content":"If multiple operations are mapped to the same RunnableEn- tity , and [SWS_Rte_04522] requires a call serialization, then a single queue is imple- mented for invocations coming from any of the operations.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:37+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002@rel:R21-11#c0a810ad","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R21-11","content":"If multiple OperationInvokedEvent s start the same RunnableEntity , and they are mapped to the same position in the same task then the RTE shall implement a single queue for invocations coming from any of the opera- tions (i.e. it ensures that the RunnableEntity implementing the server operation has completed the processing of a request before it begins processing the next request).","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:02+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002@rel:R22-11#fec4283c","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R22-11","content":"If multiple OperationInvokedEvent s or BswOperationIn- vokedEvent s start the same server ExecutableEntity , and they are mapped to the same position in the same task or ISR2 (which is enforced by [SWS_Rte_CONSTR_03873]) then the RTE shall implement a single queue for invoca- tions coming from any of the operations (i.e. it ensures that the ExecutableEntity implementing the server operation has completed the processing of a request before it begins processing the next request).","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:23+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002@rel:R25-11#b8d9db43","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","release":"R25-11","content":"Upstream requirements: SRS_Rte_00019, SRS_Rte_00033 If multiple OperationInvokedEvent s or BswOperationInvokedEvent s start the same server ExecutableEntity , and they are mapped to the same position in the same task or ISR2 (which is enforced by [SWS_Rte_CONSTR_03873]) then the RTE shall implement a single queue for invocations coming from any of the operations (i.e. it ensures that the ExecutableEntity implementing the server operation has completed the processing of a request before it begins processing the next request).","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_CP_SWS_RTE.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T09:59:14+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Rte_08002","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R25-11"],"presence_only":["R23-11","R24-11